Subject: [PATCH 3/6] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 2, patch 3;
 built on e6298271a with series 1 applied): THE IDENTIFICATION BASELINE MUST
 BE THERE, AND IT RISES ONLY BY A RAISE RECORDED IN ITS OWN LIST (the seat's
 planted case PV10). The ratchet ran only if its baseline file existed: with
 docs/IDENTIFICATION_BASELINE.json deleted, three unearned rows went in and
 the gate passed. The baseline must now be there and hold a count; a file that
 holds none is said in plain words, where the old gate crashed on one. THE
 GATE'S OWN STATED RULE IS NOW READ: it says the baseline is raised
 'DELIBERATELY with a dated reason', and the file already keeps such raises in
 a list (_baseline_raises) that nothing read. Against the baseline as it was
 at the anchor: no raise recorded then has left the list or changed; each
 raise recorded since has a date, a reason and goes up; and the baseline is no
 higher than those raises account for. It may fall freely. A raise made by
 name is counted in the gate's sentence. And no row leaves the ledger without
 a record (patch 1's rule). Main's own lock on the ratchet, which plants a row
 through the gate's reader, passes unchanged. The gate reads the past and
 joins the table. The lock: five tests added to
 tests/test_nothing_leaves_a_ledger.py; on the commit before, all five fail,
 the first because the gate passes with its baseline deleted. 0 of 19.

